From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:03:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U25 review: the same instrument, a crawlable body that
 names no hidden essay, a 44px crumb

- Politics short answer: the temptation "can fuse" faith with the nation on
  the right, as it "can make" a platform the measure of faithfulness on the
  left; one side was stated as fact and the other hedged.
- Prerendered topic bodies leave out the essay slots, so a crawler never
  reads the title and first line of a lead that is not public (the page
  shows its stand-in). The /topics listing picks a stand-in only for a row
  to an essay, the same rule as lib/topics rowTarget.
- validate-topics: a standIn on a row that does not open an essay fails
  (the page would never open it); seeded case added to the gate test.
- The "Topics" crumb above each topic's question is a 44px target without
  moving the layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
